      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix recurring Claude Keychain prompts",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- enforce a production credential-ownership boundary so CodexBar never reads Claude Code's foreign Keychain item\n- preserve persisted explicit OAuth by trying app-owned credentials first, then using the authenticated Claude owner CLI only when those credentials are exactly absent\n- keep selected token accounts and CLI-runtime OAuth authoritative, while leaving Auto as CLI then Web\n- add redacted Release/live verification plus focused routing, cache, account-isolation, and prompt-safety coverage\n\n## Root cause\n\nClaude Code owns and periodically replaces `Claude Code-credentials`, including its ACL. CodexBar was a foreign reader, so “Always Allow” only lasted until Claude replaced that item. Prompt settings changed timing, not ownership.\n\nThe ownership fix correctly removed the unsafe read, but persisted explicit OAuth still assumed CodexBar could directly load the token. On installations where the token exists only in Claude-owned storage, that produced `OAuth credentials not found` even though `claude auth status` reported a valid session. No prompt-mode setting could repair that authority mismatch.\n\n## Behavior after this change\n\n- Direct OAuth still has first priority for environment, profile-file, and CodexBar-owned cached credentials.\n- Only the typed `notFound` result may use Claude's authenticated owner CLI for usage.\n- Malformed, invalid, expired/refresh, missing-scope, temporarily unavailable cache, service, network, and cancellation errors remain terminal.\n- Selected token accounts never fall through to ambient credentials.\n- CLI-runtime explicit OAuth remains direct and actionable.\n- Auto remains CLI → Web and never adds OAuth.\n- Explicit OAuth never falls through to Web.\n\nThis removes the recurring password prompt without removing source modes, account isolation, Web fallback in Auto, or direct OAuth support.\n\n## Commit structure\n\n1. `Fix recurring Claude Keychain prompts` — credential ownership boundary and prompt root cause\n2. `Preserve explicit Claude OAuth routing` — persisted-setting compatibility and diagnostics\n3. `Fallback missing Claude OAuth to owner CLI` — exact-absence owner-mediated recovery\n\nThese are intentionally separate commits in one PR because they are independently reviewable layers of the same end-to-end regression.\n\n## Verification\n\n- exact-head redacted live Release proof for `3d0dc5e09f71df5887c446fb79e1412f0bea41da` is attached in a PR comment\n- focused ownership/routing/account/cache/debug matrix: 115 tests across 15 suites passed\n- opt-in live owner-path/auth matrix: 2 tests in 1 suite passed\n- live logged-in owner-mediated usage fetch: exit 0, no timeout\n- all 4 first-party Release executables: 0 known foreign-reader markers\n- live process/log audit: 0 unowned Security descendants and 0 attributable authorization events\n- SwiftFormat: 0 changed files need formatting\n- SwiftLint strict: 0 violations in changed Swift files\n- shell syntax and diff checks pass\n- `make check` passes except for the repository's existing Node 25 `docs/site.js` CommonJS-mode check; equivalent ESM-mode syntax validation passes\n- exact clean-source `make test` isolates one unrelated, date-sensitive existing failure in `SpendDashboardControllerTests.swift:495`; all Claude-focused tests pass. A local stabilization for that test remains deliberately uncommitted and outside this PR.\n\nFollow-up to #1844\n",
        "branch": "fix/claude-keychain-ownership",
